First Author: Ismail
Title: Artificial intelligence-driven automated lung sizing from chest radiographs
Source number: 21  ￼

Very short summary: This pilot study developed a deep-learning and computer-vision system to automate lung size measurement from portable chest radiographs for transplant size matching. Five key findings were: (1) the validation cohort included 50 lung transplant recipients; (2) the framework used a 2-step pipeline with lung-mask segmentation followed by automated feature-point detection; (3) the system generated 6 standardized lung height/width measurements; (4) average measurement error versus the mean of 2 radiologists was <2.5% (<7.0 mm); and (5) agreement between AI and radiologists was very high, with Pearson correlation 0.97 and intraclass correlations generally 0.95–0.99. Figures 1–3 and Tables 1–2 were used directly for this extraction.  ￼

